# G2 Continuous Curvature & Squircle Geometry

In precision industrial design (such as luxury automotive contours) and modern operating systems (such as Apple macOS / iOS), curvature continuity directly dictates the softness of light reflection.

## Geometric Continuity Orders

Geometric continuity defines the smoothness at the junction of two curves:

- **$G^0$ Continuity (Positional)**: The curves touch at the junction, but their tangents diverge abruptly (a 90-degree corner).
- **$G^1$ Continuity (Tangential)**: The curves share the same tangent vector at the junction, making first derivatives continuous. Standard CSS `border-radius` is a classic $G^1$ fillet (straight lines tangent to quarter circles).
- **$G^2$ Continuity (Curvature)**: The curves share the exact same curvature $\kappa$ across the junction, making second derivatives continuous.

## Why Circular Fillets Break Visual Continuity

For a standard circular fillet:
- The straight edge has zero curvature ($\kappa = 0$).
- Entering the circle instantaneously jumps curvature to $\kappa = \frac{1}{R}$.
This second-derivative jump causes an optical crease under specular lighting or refraction (the Specular Break phenomenon).

## The Superellipse Formula and Apple Smooth Corners

Apple transitioned to the superellipse (Lamé curve) starting with iOS 7:
$$\left| \frac{x}{a} \right|^n + \left| \frac{y}{b} \right|^n = 1 \quad (n \approx 4 \sim 5)$$
By introducing an Euler spiral (Clothoid) transition between the flat edge and the corner, the rate of curvature change at the transition point stays exactly zero.

## TuffEx Engineering Implementation

In the Web and Electron environment, TuffEx implements G2 squircle corners through progressive enhancement:

:::TuffCodeBlock{lang="scss"}
---
code: |
  @mixin tx-squircle($radius: 16px) {
    @supports (corner-shape: squircle) {
      border-radius: $radius;
      corner-shape: squircle;
    }
    @supports not (corner-shape: squircle) {
      border-radius: $radius;
      // Fitted smooth bezier curves or SVG Mask delivering superellipse profiles
      clip-path: url("data:image/svg+xml,...");
    }
  }
---
:::

On large floating cards and CoreBox windows, G2 continuity eliminates harsh corner breaks and ensures refracted borders merge seamlessly into the canvas.
